docs: spec v2.1, build plan v1.2, ADRs, and the Obsidian vault

Establishes docs/ as the single source of truth for the build, linked so
Obsidian renders the decision graph.

Documents:
- functional-spec.md    v2.1 (was v2.0) - demo-vs-production audit applied
- build-plan.md         v1.2 (73 chunks; +P1-19 colour discipline)
- spec-change-register.md  26 changes: 8 Critical, 11 High, 7 Medium
- design/dashboard-kpi-design.md  governs board/committee surfaces
- decisions/ADR-001..011  every decision, with what it overrides and why
- index.md              map of content and current build status

Two rulings applied to the spec in this commit:
- Obligation <-> Control is now many-to-many (was 1:many). One duty often
  needs several controls acting together; widening after seed data exists
  would be a migration, not an edit. ADR-009.
- Audit Committee Chair loses close authority on speak-up reports and
  fraud cases, contradicting section 4.7 ("a chair reviews; they do not
  operate the platform"). Statutory read access is untouched - access to
  read is not authority to dispose. ADR-010.

New chunk P1-19 addresses the colour scheme. The palette is already a
correct semantic token set; the defect is DOMAIN_COLORS, a six-hue raw-hex
rainbow applied to a categorical attribute inside dense tables. Colour is
confined to state; categorical hues stay inside visualisations. The Home
enterprise risk heat map is explicitly retained as built.

All 15 wikilink targets resolve. No BR-*, G-* or workflow identifier was
renumbered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
